WEBVTT

01:50.989 --> 01:52.190
Block: [roaring punch]

02:02.211 --> 02:04.616
Enough messing around!

02:12.398 --> 02:14.536
Crocodine: Howl, Vortex Axe!

02:15.672 --> 02:17.274
Take this!

02:20.213 --> 02:23.386
I shall be your
opponent, young mage.

02:23.419 --> 02:26.292
Well, you're going to have to
catch me first, aren't you?

02:34.743 --> 02:35.778
[snarling]

02:47.134 --> 02:49.204
[charging roar]

03:12.050 --> 03:15.625
Hadlar: So... this is the
power of the Dragonoid...

03:15.658 --> 03:18.797
A truly worthy
opponent, aren't you?!

03:30.120 --> 03:33.192
You still don't seem
to understand...

03:33.226 --> 03:35.564
It's over!

03:58.611 --> 04:03.153
Baran: A Dragonoid will not stop
until its opponent is destroyed.

04:03.186 --> 04:06.927
This is the ultimate
battle form of my kind.

04:09.231 --> 04:11.536
And now that I have
unleashed this power...

04:11.570 --> 04:13.072
you don't stand a chance -

04:13.106 --> 04:15.811
no matter how
hard you might try!

04:26.132 --> 04:27.602
C-Curse you!

04:34.782 --> 04:39.191
[pained howl]

04:39.224 --> 04:41.396
Now you can't use that sword.

04:41.429 --> 04:44.468
Difficult to cast
spells, too, isn't it?

04:46.272 --> 04:49.278
Hadlar [thought]:
He's strong... Too strong!

04:49.311 --> 04:51.549
The Superior Being
body was created

04:51.583 --> 04:53.687
based on the
Dragonoid's abilities.

04:53.720 --> 04:58.330
It should rival or even
surpass his might...

04:58.363 --> 05:03.439
So, why? Why can't
I do anything to him?!

05:06.012 --> 05:07.347
Mystvearn: Such power...

05:07.380 --> 05:10.654
Even Hadlar is
no match for him.

05:10.688 --> 05:15.898
It seems that our friend has
disturbed the hornet's nest.

05:15.932 --> 05:18.102
The Dragon Knight
is no different from

05:18.136 --> 05:20.440
any other beast in nature.

05:20.474 --> 05:22.612
They'll display
incredible strength

05:22.645 --> 05:27.622
to protect their offspring,
and punish any transgression.

05:27.655 --> 05:30.595
Baran can't control himself.

05:30.628 --> 05:34.937
I suppose... that
settles things, then.

05:34.970 --> 05:36.506
Regrettable.

05:37.709 --> 05:40.380
Mystvearn: You're going
to detonate the Black Core?

05:40.414 --> 05:42.953
Hadlar already
lost this battle

05:42.986 --> 05:46.326
and I believe he has
earned some kind of mercy.

05:46.359 --> 05:48.095
Has he not?

05:49.967 --> 05:54.141
All I need to do is unleash a
finger's worth of magic power...

05:54.175 --> 05:56.680
and the Core will explode.

05:56.713 --> 06:01.189
The next move Baran
makes against Hadlar...

06:01.222 --> 06:04.796
Will be his final one.

06:16.853 --> 06:21.162
Well, it seems the Dark Lord
still has some fight left.

06:21.195 --> 06:23.534
[pained snarl]

06:23.567 --> 06:27.041
You would seriously attempt
an Ultra Combustion Slash

06:27.074 --> 06:28.744
with a broken arm?

06:29.278 --> 06:30.981
It's futile!

06:34.021 --> 06:35.758
Well, futile or otherwise...

06:35.792 --> 06:41.435
Accepting my fate without trying
would be worse than this pain.

06:41.469 --> 06:46.145
I will not back down.
Not after all I've done!

06:47.481 --> 06:48.951
Very well.

06:50.454 --> 06:52.490
I'm waiting, Hadlar.

07:08.290 --> 07:12.197
[roaring]

07:12.231 --> 07:14.702
[growling]

07:18.209 --> 07:20.915
[roaring]

07:20.949 --> 07:23.486
[snarling]

07:55.551 --> 07:58.991
Hadlar: [grim chuckle]

07:59.024 --> 08:02.999
How disappointing
it is, Baran, truly...

08:03.032 --> 08:10.714
To come so far, yet still
wind... up... short....

08:14.054 --> 08:19.064
Vearn: Your final effort
was most impressive, Hadlar.

08:19.097 --> 08:20.734
But never fear;

08:20.768 --> 08:22.638
Just as you hoped...

08:22.671 --> 08:24.609
your demise can
still bring about

08:24.643 --> 08:27.548
the Dragon Knight's
annihilation.

08:27.581 --> 08:31.388
Your moment of glory arrives.

08:31.421 --> 08:34.896
Now reveal your
fury, Black Core!

08:43.346 --> 08:44.715
What's this?

08:47.622 --> 08:48.890
But, how?!

08:48.924 --> 08:52.899
I cast my magic power,
and yet nothing happened...

08:52.932 --> 08:55.437
Why didn't the Core detonate?

08:55.470 --> 08:56.973
Baran: [chuckling]

08:58.008 --> 09:01.248
You underestimated
me, Dark King.

09:02.619 --> 09:03.854
Why do you think...

09:03.887 --> 09:09.064
that I accepted Hadlar's
final challenge, you fool?

09:09.098 --> 09:13.907
This moment - I was waiting
for this very moment.

09:16.278 --> 09:20.621
So I could contain the Core's
blast with my Draconic Aura!

09:24.362 --> 09:26.432
Very clever, Baran.

09:26.466 --> 09:30.574
So, he was prepared
for the explosion.

09:33.446 --> 09:34.314
What...

09:35.183 --> 09:36.218
What...

09:36.252 --> 09:38.624
What is that thing?

09:38.657 --> 09:42.063
And what was it doing
inside my body?!

09:42.097 --> 09:47.207
You are a Darkling, you must
have heard of these before.

09:47.240 --> 09:49.411
This is a Black Core.

09:49.444 --> 09:51.281
A Black Core?!

09:52.183 --> 09:55.390
Hadlar: That's...
That's impossible!

09:55.423 --> 09:58.362
a cursed legendary
explosive...

09:58.396 --> 10:01.435
It was inside
of me all this time?

10:01.468 --> 10:04.475
Who... Who would
do such a thing?!

10:04.509 --> 10:06.279
Who do you think it was?

10:06.312 --> 10:07.749
It was your king.

10:07.782 --> 10:10.788
The one who promised
you the surface world,

10:10.821 --> 10:13.661
all the while
intending to destroy it-

10:13.694 --> 10:15.965
and you in the process!

10:15.998 --> 10:17.969
K-King Vearn?

10:18.002 --> 10:19.170
I see...

10:19.204 --> 10:22.243
So, all this time you and
Dai were holding back because

10:22.277 --> 10:26.385
you feared you might indirectly
set off the Black Core...

10:27.822 --> 10:33.165
What happened... What happened
to having a fair fight?

10:33.199 --> 10:38.677
There was no way you could
have won under such conditions.

10:38.710 --> 10:42.919
I sacrificed my own body...

10:42.952 --> 10:47.093
I sacrificed my life
to have this battle!

10:49.031 --> 10:52.136
[howling]

10:55.143 --> 10:56.846
Mystvearn: Hadlar...

10:59.051 --> 11:02.859
Killvearn: Oh, my.
How very pathetic.

11:02.892 --> 11:05.765
Vearn: It can't be
helped, Killvearn.

11:05.798 --> 11:08.571
I didn't expect the
power of Baran's Aura

11:08.604 --> 11:12.611
to be this strong
in the Dragonoid form.

11:12.645 --> 11:16.285
And yet he managed to
repel my Magic Power.

11:16.319 --> 11:18.222
How very impressive.

11:18.256 --> 11:20.193
But as the Core's creator,

11:20.226 --> 11:23.533
all I need to do is get
near enough to the device

11:23.567 --> 11:26.806
to trigger the
detonation sequence.

11:31.048 --> 11:32.250
So be it.

11:32.283 --> 11:37.294
I shall go there myself and
erase them along with the Core.

11:37.327 --> 11:40.768
Killvearn: But, my king...
if you go out there,

11:40.801 --> 11:43.774
you're going to make
the rest of us look bad!

11:43.807 --> 11:45.811
Right, Myst?

11:45.844 --> 11:47.615
[amused chuckle]

11:47.648 --> 11:49.719
And there he goes.

11:53.492 --> 11:56.599
Baran - wh-what are you doing?

11:56.632 --> 11:58.135
Removing the Core
from your body

11:58.169 --> 12:01.008
before Vearn can
make his next move!

12:02.745 --> 12:06.051
[agonized howl]

12:10.393 --> 12:11.796
Hadlar: Mystvearn?

12:11.830 --> 12:14.802
He's only here
to try and stop me.

12:15.571 --> 12:17.340
Is it true?

12:17.374 --> 12:22.116
D-Do you... Do you
share King Vearn's will?!

12:22.150 --> 12:25.223
Have you come
to cast me aside...

12:25.256 --> 12:27.460
Like some broken tool?

12:27.494 --> 12:33.139
Is that it? Was I nothing
more than a pawn to you, too?!

12:33.172 --> 12:38.516
Mystvearn: Hadlar, we both know
the answer to that question.

12:46.231 --> 12:51.041
Mystvearn: The Dark King's plan
takes precedence above all.

12:53.345 --> 12:57.788
Hadlar: I see.
So... this is the end.

12:57.821 --> 13:00.894
Well, Mystvearn, it seems
you're already too late.

13:00.928 --> 13:05.036
Even with you here I cannot
be defeated in battle!

13:05.069 --> 13:06.907
Mystvearn: Don't be so sure.

13:06.940 --> 13:09.879
I need not dirty
my hands with combat-

13:09.912 --> 13:13.887
I can erase the
both of you without it.

13:17.728 --> 13:20.901
W-What - what kind
of power could this be?!

13:20.934 --> 13:25.076
Mystvearn: King Vearn,
do I have your permission?

13:25.110 --> 13:28.315
Indeed. Do it, Mystvearn.

14:16.478 --> 14:17.849
Th-That's...

14:17.882 --> 14:20.219
Mystvearn's true form?!

14:22.257 --> 14:23.425
Yes, now...

14:23.459 --> 14:26.999
Time to embrace the
annihilation of the Black Core!

14:32.645 --> 14:34.949
The device is fully active!

14:34.982 --> 14:36.619
Baran [thought]: Impossible!

14:36.653 --> 14:41.529
My Dragonoid Draconic Aura
should repel any Magic Power.

14:41.562 --> 14:44.100
It would take the presence
of King Vearn himself,

14:44.134 --> 14:46.672
at close proximity,
to do that...

14:48.676 --> 14:50.279
Then that means-

14:50.313 --> 14:51.616
Detonate!

15:00.668 --> 15:01.936
It's going to explode!

15:01.970 --> 15:03.941
It makes no sense at all.

15:03.974 --> 15:06.513
Only the Magic Power
of a Black Core's creator

15:06.546 --> 15:08.382
should be able to detonate it.

15:08.415 --> 15:12.524
Mystvearn, does this mean
that your real form...?

15:12.558 --> 15:14.862
There is no point asking.

15:14.895 --> 15:18.904
In mere moments,
you will both be erased.

15:18.937 --> 15:21.241
Now that you have
seen this face,

15:21.275 --> 15:24.515
you cannot be
allowed to survive.

15:42.384 --> 15:45.456
This is more than
just an earthquake.

15:45.489 --> 15:46.660
Something nearby -

15:46.693 --> 15:49.532
something nearby is
causing this disturbance!

15:49.565 --> 15:51.301
Turn and face me, you fool!

15:56.412 --> 15:58.348
Hyunckel: Everybody,
we need to regroup!

15:58.382 --> 16:00.620
Something's happening
to the Field of Death.

16:07.000 --> 16:08.302
What the...?

16:10.974 --> 16:13.513
[troubled scream]

16:13.547 --> 16:15.784
What is it?! Merle?

16:15.818 --> 16:18.222
A dark force
swallowing everything...

16:18.255 --> 16:20.560
Everyone... will vanish.

16:20.594 --> 16:22.197
Even Popp.

16:22.230 --> 16:23.567
No...

16:23.600 --> 16:24.635
Amy: Calm down.

16:24.668 --> 16:28.041
Merle: [crying]

16:31.682 --> 16:34.420
Could that be what's
causing this earthquake?

16:34.889 --> 16:35.657
Princess!

16:35.691 --> 16:36.659
Emergency!

16:37.862 --> 16:40.901
Something strange is happening
around the Field of Death.

16:40.934 --> 16:44.241
It's like...
an active volcano!

16:44.274 --> 16:45.042
What?!

16:45.075 --> 16:47.480
The others must be
in grave danger.

16:51.255 --> 16:52.290
Princess, please...

16:52.323 --> 16:54.695
We must go save the Heroes!

16:55.597 --> 16:56.599
Flora: Enough.

16:58.369 --> 16:59.370
W-Who...?

17:03.580 --> 17:05.016
I know you!

17:05.049 --> 17:07.454
I... I can't
believe you're here!

17:07.487 --> 17:10.727
Flora: We must leave this
place immediately. Hurry.

17:11.428 --> 17:12.396
All: Right!

17:18.877 --> 17:22.751
Baran [thought]: It's no good.
The explosion is inevitable.

17:25.023 --> 17:28.429
Goodbye, Hadlar and Baran.

17:28.462 --> 17:32.337
The king himself
respected both of you.

17:32.370 --> 17:36.646
And now your names shall
be etched upon my heart...

17:36.679 --> 17:38.650
forevermore.

17:43.793 --> 17:45.530
[pained groan]

18:08.676 --> 18:10.112
[startled cries]

18:21.435 --> 18:23.038
Killvearn: This shaking...

18:23.072 --> 18:26.211
Is the palace finally
going to reveal itself?

18:26.244 --> 18:28.281
That's correct.

18:36.264 --> 18:38.035
Killvearn: Covering up already?

18:38.068 --> 18:41.107
Your true face is so
much more interesting.

18:41.141 --> 18:43.379
Yeah - let's get
another look at 'ya!

18:43.412 --> 18:47.487
Mystvearn's power should not be
exposed without good reason.

18:47.521 --> 18:50.293
Mystvearn: As you
command, my Dark King.

18:50.326 --> 18:54.669
You've done well indeed.
Good, Mystvearn.

18:54.702 --> 18:57.808
It's done. All of it.

18:57.842 --> 19:00.146
The Hero and his
band of traitors

19:00.179 --> 19:02.818
have all been
erased at last...

19:02.851 --> 19:05.323
along with the Field of Death.

19:05.356 --> 19:07.661
Killvearn: So,
we're all that remains.

19:07.694 --> 19:14.975
Right. Just us three...
and my mighty palace, as well.

19:15.008 --> 19:19.985
It is finally time for the
surface world to be erased.

19:20.019 --> 19:22.591
[victorious cackle]

19:22.625 --> 19:27.066
I'm removing the barrier
around our new base now.

19:27.099 --> 19:30.206
The rock that obscured
it is falling away,

19:30.239 --> 19:32.444
revealing our vessel.

19:32.477 --> 19:35.315
But I sense something amiss.

19:37.119 --> 19:39.558
Vearn: After the
Black Core's explosion,

19:39.592 --> 19:42.330
everything aside
from our stronghold

19:42.363 --> 19:45.436
should have been reduced
to nothing but ash.

19:47.975 --> 19:49.745
Could it be?

19:49.778 --> 19:53.085
Mystvearn, have the
Heyedras search the area

19:53.118 --> 19:55.390
for any possible survivors.

19:55.423 --> 19:56.725
Mystvearn: Yes, sire.

20:14.595 --> 20:15.462
[gasping]

20:15.496 --> 20:18.435
Heyedra: Survivors!
Survivors spotted!

20:18.468 --> 20:20.741
Four of them on the left wing.

20:20.774 --> 20:23.178
The Disciples of Avan.

20:23.212 --> 20:26.920
Mystvearn: They survived?
In that explosion?

20:26.953 --> 20:28.255
[chuckling]

20:28.288 --> 20:32.631
My, my - how very
fortunate they all must feel.

20:32.665 --> 20:34.434
Hyunckel: I can't
believe we made it.

20:34.467 --> 20:36.705
That explosion
was unbelievable.

20:37.240 --> 20:38.510
Maam: Who saved us?

20:38.543 --> 20:40.747
Popp: Probably
Crocodine, right?

20:40.781 --> 20:42.651
I mean, who else has
the brute strength

20:42.684 --> 20:45.524
to save us all by
burying us alive?

20:45.557 --> 20:50.099
Stop complaining.
The point is, we're still alive.

20:50.133 --> 20:54.441
I figured that going underground
would shield us from the blast.

20:54.474 --> 20:58.783
So I dug a hole that was
big enough to hide all of us.

20:58.816 --> 20:59.952
Good thinking-

20:59.985 --> 21:02.558
I don't think we could have
survived that, otherwise.

21:02.591 --> 21:05.430
It seems like the
Royal Guard are gone.

21:05.463 --> 21:08.870
We must be the only
ones who actually made it.

21:09.806 --> 21:10.774
[awkward chuckling]

21:10.807 --> 21:12.210
Well, good call!

21:12.243 --> 21:13.278
Yeah, too late.

21:15.016 --> 21:17.220
But, uh... where are we?

21:17.253 --> 21:19.424
It doesn't look
like the Field of Death.

21:19.457 --> 21:22.463
My guess - we're on
top of Vearn Palace.

21:22.496 --> 21:24.467
The blast destroyed the Field,

21:24.500 --> 21:27.072
and exposed what
was hidden underground.

21:27.106 --> 21:30.514
Well, then... that structure
over there must be...

21:30.547 --> 21:33.553
Hyunckel: It must be
the palace's true form.

21:40.901 --> 21:41.803
No way.

21:41.836 --> 21:43.038
Maam: Popp?

21:44.509 --> 21:47.046
Popp [thought]: You're saying
we that just flew into the sky

21:47.080 --> 21:48.916
with Vearn Palace?!

21:56.699 --> 22:01.074
[stunned breath]

23:37.667 --> 23:39.939
Narrator: With Vearn
Palace's true from revealed

23:39.972 --> 23:42.544
after the Black Core's
devastating blast,

23:42.578 --> 23:44.949
the Disciples of
Avan search for Dai,

23:44.982 --> 23:47.621
but instead they find
the horrifying results of

23:47.655 --> 23:50.426
Hadlar and Baran's battle.

23:50.459 --> 23:52.496
And before they can
plot their next move,

23:52.530 --> 23:56.572
the merciless King Vearn
makes his instead...

23:56.606 --> 23:58.308
So don't miss
the next episode of

23:58.341 --> 24:00.581
Dragon Quest:
The Adventure of Dai,

24:00.614 --> 24:03.018
"The Inherited Heart".
